# Play Console Walkthrough — {{ app.name }}

A step-by-step guide to publishing **{{ app.name }}** on Google Play.

---

## 1. Create App

Go to [Play Console](https://play.google.com/console) and click **Create app**.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| App name | **{{ app.name }}** |
| Default language | **English (United States)** |
| App or Game | **{{ 'Game' if content_rating.is_game | default(false) else 'App' }}** |
| Free or Paid | **{{ 'Paid' if app.is_paid | default(false) else 'Free' }}** |

Check all declaration boxes (Developer Program Policies, US export laws, etc.) and click **Create app**.

---

## 2. Store Listing

Navigate to: **Grow → Store presence → Main store listing**

Fill in all fields using the **Store Listing Guide** (`store-listing-guide.md`):
- Short description ({{ app.description_short | default('TODO') | length if app.description_short is defined else '?' }} chars)
- Full description
- App icon (512×512)
- Feature graphic (1024×500)
- Phone screenshots (min 2)
- App category: **{{ app.category | default('TODO') }}**
- Contact details

---

## 3. Content Rating

Navigate to: **Policy → App content → Content rating**

Click **Start new questionnaire** and answer each question using the **Content Rating Answers** guide (`content-rating-answers.md`).

Expected result: **Rated for Everyone** (based on your config).

---

## 4. Target Audience

Navigate to: **Policy → App content → Target audience**

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Target age group | **{{ app.target_audience | default('general') | title }}** |
{% if app.target_audience | default('general') == 'general' %}

Select **18 and over** (or your applicable age group). If your app is not specifically designed for children, do NOT select any under-13 age group — doing so triggers additional compliance requirements (COPPA / Families Policy).
{% elif app.target_audience | default('general') == 'children' %}

⚠️ **Children's app** — you must comply with Google's Families Policy:
- No behavioral advertising
- Teacher Approved program (optional but recommended)
- Privacy policy must explicitly address children's data
{% endif %}

---

## 5. App Access

Navigate to: **Policy → App content → App access**

{% if 'auth' in firebase.services | default([]) %}
Your app **requires sign-in** (Firebase Auth). You must select **"All or some functionality is restricted"** and provide test credentials.

### Test Account Setup

1. Create a test account for Google reviewers:
   - Email: `playstore-reviewer@{{ app.developer_email.split('@')[1] | default('yourdomain.com') }}` (or any email you control)
   - Password: Use a strong, unique password
2. In Play Console, click **Add new instructions**:
   - Name: **Test Account**
   - Username: (the test email)
   - Password: (the test password)
   - Any other instructions: e.g., "Tap 'Sign in with email' and enter these credentials"
{% if app.test_account_notes is defined %}
3. Additional notes: {{ app.test_account_notes }}
{% endif %}

⚠️ **The test account must work** — a non-functional test account is the #1 reason for review rejection.
{% else %}
Your app does not require sign-in. Select **"All functionality is available without special access"**.
{% endif %}

